{"name":"Stunning Sapphire","hex":"#185887","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stunning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an effect that stuns.","Exceptionally beautiful or attractive."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of stun"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stunning"},{"term":"sapphire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clear deep blue variety of corundum, valued as a precious stone.","A white, yellow, or purple variety of corundum, either clear or translucent."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["of a deep blue colour.","pertaining to a 45th year"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sapphire"}],"entries":[{"title":"Stunning","blocks":[{"text":"Stunning is the process of rendering animals immobile or unconscious, with or without killing the animal, when or immediately prior to slaughtering them for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Medieval_pig_slaughter.jpg/330px-Medieval_pig_slaughter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stunning"},{"title":"Sapphire","blocks":[{"text":"Sapphire is a gemstone variety of the mineral corundum, the crystalline form of aluminium oxide (α-Al2O3). Pure corundum is colorless, while trace elements in its crystal structure produce a wide range of colors. Blue is the best-known, but sapphires also occur in yellow, green, purple, pink, orange, gray, black, and colorless forms. Red gem-quality corundum is classified as ruby rather than sapphire. The boundary between ruby and pink sapphire is based on color appearance and varies among gemological and trade conventions. Sapphire has a Mohs hardness of 9, making it highly resistant to scratching and abrasion."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Logan_Sapphire_10956420_cropped.png/330px-Logan_Sapphire_10956420_cropped.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sapphire"},{"title":"Shades of blue","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color blue may differ in hue, chroma, or lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a blue or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Shades_of_Blue.svg/330px-Shades_of_Blue.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/37/Richardson%27s_abattoir.jpg/500px-Richardson%27s_abattoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/37/Richardson%27s_abattoir.jpg/1280px-Richardson%27s_abattoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/37/Richardson%27s_abattoir.jpg/500px-Richardson%27s_abattoir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blueprint for a slaughterhouse designed by Benjamin Ward Richardson, published 1908.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARichardson's_abattoir.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cattle_Market-_Everyday_Life_at_Cattle_Markets_in_Kent%2C_England%2C_UK%2C_1944_D22206.jpg/500px-Cattle_Market-_Everyday_Life_at_Cattle_Markets_in_Kent%2C_England%2C_UK%2C_1944_D22206.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cattle_Market-_Everyday_Life_at_Cattle_Markets_in_Kent%2C_England%2C_UK%2C_1944_D22206.jpg/500px-Cattle_Market-_Everyday_Life_at_Cattle_Markets_in_Kent%2C_En